   "daf": "44a",
   "sentenceId": 17,
   "he": "הַצִּומֵּם וְהַצִּומֵּעַ. תָּנָא: אַף הַצִּימֵּחַ. לָא הֲווֹ יָדְעִי רַבָּנַן מַאי ״צִימֵּחַ״, שְׁמַעוּ לְהָהוּא טַיָּיעָא דַּהֲוָה קָאָמַר: ״מַאן דְּבָעֵי צִימֵּחַ״, וְאִישְׁתְּכַח גַּדְיָא חֲזִיזָא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna also taught that «the tzomem and the tzome’a» are blemished. The Sages «taught» in a baraita: «The tzime’aḥ» is «also» disqualified from performing the Temple service. «The Sages did not know what a tzime’aḥ» is. «They heard a certain Arab who was saying: Who wants a tzime’aḥ, and it was found» to be «a long-eared goat.»"
  }
